  "description": "Elmville is a stunning new development in Harold’s Cross, a much sought-after address on Dublin’s south side. Beginning at the Robert Emmet Bridge on the Grand Canal and only a 20-minute walk from the city centre, Harold’s Cross is a lively and bustling suburb with an excellent public transport service.\n\nElmville fits right in with the energy and vibrancy of Harold’s Cross. Inside the private gated development, the structural design utilises wood and exposed brick, marrying beautifully with its surrounding communal green landscape.\n\nAll apartments are large and enjoy a flood of natural light through floor-to-ceiling sliding doors, leading on to a private balcony or patio area. What makes this development stand out is that each apartment has been fitted out with a unique interior design finish. Each apartment has been thoughtfully finished to a high standard with bespoke design solutions in every apartment.\n\nThere is carpet flooring throughout all hallways and bedrooms with wood effect tiles in the kitchen / living / dining gives the apartments a high-end luxurious feel. Each apartment is provided with an office desk and chair for modern living styles. The attention to detail in Elmville allows residents the opportunity to unwind and settle down in their new home.\n\nEvery residence at Elmville is equipped with an intercom, generous storage space and air-source heat-pumps to ensure high energy efficiency and low running costs. There is secure underground parking and residents also benefit from ample bike storage facilities.\n\nHarold’s Cross is stylish, trendy, and steeped in history, the village is home to an eclectic mix of restaurants, pubs and things-to-do. The sense of community is as strong as ever and the park hosts an annual festival with live entertainment, arts and crafts and fun for all the family. Harold’s Cross boasts some beautiful architecture, an exciting entertainment scene and it has more than its fair share of noteworthy spots serving up delicious coffee and fresh pastries every day.\n\nThe Dublin Bus nos. 9, 16, 49, 54A and 83 all include Harold’s Cross on their routes and indeed, the endless spoils of neighbouring Rathmines and Ranelagh are within immediate reach by foot.\n\nParking is available at an additional charge.",
